      "file": "scenes/scene-1.js",
      "narration": "Your content stays yours. The look changes the framing, the motion, how text arrives, where captions sit, and the overall texture.",
      "storyboard": "Paper stage. The word 'message' sits locked in ink at the centre in 150px and never moves, our anchor. Around it the presentation changes beat by beat: on 'framing' crop marks tighten; on 'motion' a teal arc swings past; on 'how text arrives' letters cascade in; on 'captions' a caption bar slides under it; on 'texture' a grain overlay washes over. The camera holds still, so only the look changes. The bullet list is cut and rebuilt as these live demonstrations.",
      "minDuration": 10,
      "slide": {
        "title": "Look and feel changes presentation, not message",
